# Agent Infrastructure Enforcement

When you change **1+ files** under `.cursor/` that are part of the agent infrastructure (rules, skills, hooks, agent-roles, references, commands), run the `reviewing-agent-infrastructure` skill before reporting done. Write a stamp to `.cursor/hooks/state/agent-infrastructure.stamp.md`.

## Layer 1: This Rule (L2g — Advisory)

Tells you to validate. Fires when glob-matched `.cursor/` files are edited.

Skip for:
- `.cursor/hooks/state/` — runtime artifacts (stamps, hashes, scratchpads)
- `.cursor/plans/` — descriptive plan documents, not infrastructure (no enforcement, no references)

## Layer 2: Stop Hook — Grind Loop (L5 — Enforced)

`post-task-check.sh` Check 6 verifies `agent-infrastructure.stamp.md` exists and is fresh (< 10 min). If missing, it sends you back with a `followup_message` up to 3 times. You cannot finish until validation runs or the cap is hit.

## How to Validate

Follow the `reviewing-agent-infrastructure` skill checklist manually. Write a stamp to `.cursor/hooks/state/agent-infrastructure.stamp.md`.

## Triggered Rule Notice

When this rule applies, mention it early:
"This touches .cursor/ infrastructure — agent-infrastructure validation will be required."
